  "root_cause": "PackMachBase::canUnpack() iterated Mach-O load commands using a pointer into a heap buffer sized by mhdri.sizeofcmds, but it read 32-bit fields (cmd/cmdsize) via BE/LE accessors (get_ne32/get_le32) before ensuring that at least 8 bytes remained for the load_command header. A truncated final load command therefore triggered a 4-byte OOB read past the end of the allocation. A similar unchecked header read existed in the packed-header parsing loop.",
  "fix_approach": "Add minimal per-iteration minimum-size guards so we never read cmd/cmdsize unless at least 8 bytes remain in the command buffer, and treat cmdsize < 8 as invalid. Specifically: (1) harden is_bad_linker_command() to reject cmdsize < 8; (2) in canUnpack() break out of the load-command scan if headway < 8 to avoid the initial unsafe 4-byte reads; (3) in the packed-header load-command loop, throw if headway < 8 before reading cmd/cmdsize. Additionally, adjust test-mode error handling so warning-only failures (e.g., NotPacked) don’t cause a non-zero exit during secb repro.",
